 "text": "Hey, how are you holding up? Roughly eye level when you' sitting in front of it. A bit lower if it' on stand. People spend so much time looking down at their screens. It locks with a button on the side. It locks when you push the button in. Roughly one fingertip. If someone really wants to get in, they can break in, but most thief break-ins happen because the door was left unlocked. Then a small floor stand with a desk lamp on top is your friend. Use a lamp with a bright bulb. Good idea. Old books are great way to raise your monitor.",
